    "title": "Bristol Motor Speedway facility ready to go for race weekend - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Kenny Hawkins ,\n9 hours ago\nBRISTOL, Tenn. (WJHL) — Just a month ago, Bristol Motor Speedway had set a new Major League Baseball record with over 90,000 tickets sold to watch the Cincinnati Reds and Atlanta Braves play in the Speedway Classic.\nWhen they packed up and left town, they left a mess for the race track to clean up before next weekend’s Bass Pro Shops Night Race, which was part of a triple-header weekend.\nThe track had to rebuild the Goodyear building in between Turns 1 and 2, and some of the track inside the wall. But after about 30 days, everything is ready to go before the green flag drops next Thursday at the last great colosseum.\n“Major League Baseball had about 200 people here to start disassembling everything, right when the game was over,” BMS President Jerry Caldwell said. “I mean, that night, they were moving on Sunday, and then we brought in a crew of about 100 once baseball’s materials were out, and started rebuilding and working on the walls.”\nCaldwell also announced Goodyear will roll out a softer right-side tire for the Bass Pro Shops Night Race.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WJHL | Tri-Cities News & Weather.",
